      "content": "Listen up, because if you want to build a solid foundation without getting crushed by the bar, you need to treat your body like a fortress under siege, and that fortress is built on the principles of the **Goblin's Great Three**.\n\nHere is your 4-week roadmap, but I have to warn you: **Goblins** are notoriously difficult to train, and if you try to lift heavy weights without proper form, you'll end up with a broken ribcage or a twisted spine. So, listen closely to this **Goblin's Guide to Linear Progression**.\n\n### The Schedule: 4 Weeks of Goblin Strength\n*Note: This is a linear progression plan, meaning you add a tiny bit of weight every session, just like a goblin adds a coin to his hoard. Do not skip steps, or the goblins will steal your progress.*\n\n**Frequency:** 3 days per week (e.g., Mon, Wed, Fri).\n**Rest:** 2 days between sessions to let your muscles recover, just like a goblin needs time to digest his stolen gold before raiding again.\n\n#### Week 1: The Foundation (Learning the Form)\n*Focus: Mastering the movement pattern",
